+# Meeting MVP execution roadmap
+
+**Roadmap issue:** `5ffa9a58-8c81-45f3-8ca8-cbc861a0633a`
+**Date:** 2026-08-09
+**Base:** `origin/main@341caeb0072f6642ce9b2172c1d092f91bcd3265`
+**Classification:** Critical cross-lane execution plan; authorization, migrations, durable finalization, and explicit work creation
+**Status:** PLAN synthesis; no implementation, push, PR, database operation, issue closure, or stage advance authorized
+
+## Product outcome
+
+The MVP is one reliable local-meeting loop:
+
+```text
+local meeting completes
+  -> canonical final summary becomes visible and adjustable
+  -> compact action candidates appear
+  -> human chooses Add, Adjust, or Dismiss
+  -> only Add creates exactly one Product-Suite work item
+```
+
+Nothing else is required to call this MVP complete. Extraction, finalization,
+models, refresh, retries, agents, calendars, or providers never create a task or
+work item automatically. A summary has Adjust and Dismiss but no Add. An action
+candidate has Add, Adjust, and Dismiss. Missing owner, date, parent, dependency,
+team, or status evidence is omitted or blocks Add; it is never guessed.
+
+The MVP uses local capture only. Requested visual artifacts, Recall/Zoom/Meet/
+Teams adapters, omnipresent agent chat, and an agent-editable canvas are future
+lanes. They remain visible in the roadmap so they do not disappear, but they do
+not delay the local transcript-to-work-item outcome.
+
