+## Exact human flow
+
+1. The user starts local capture after the existing explicit consent/recording
+   indicator contract is satisfied. The client persists the capture-session ID
+   and monotonic transcript sequence.
+2. On Stop, the client drains through the last contiguous acknowledged segment
+   and submits one stable terminal event. Retry/reconnect reuses its identity.
+3. The server commits `completed`, final chapters, and the canonical summary
+   artifact/version once. Failure leaves the last complete artifact visible and
+   reports retryable finalization; the UI does not claim success.
+4. After refresh, the user sees a summary card and action-candidate cards. The
+   summary card exposes Adjust and Dismiss only. Pending action cards expose Add,
+   Adjust, and Dismiss. Each card has a visible type/icon, concise title, one
+   source line, and at most three verified owner/date/parent/dependency chips or
+   links; missing evidence is absent.
+5. Summary Adjust opens an inline labelled textarea. The returned structured
+   version becomes current only after the expected-version CAS wins. Dismiss
+   hides the summary from review without deleting meeting evidence; Restore is
+   explicit.
+6. Action Adjust uses free text or one of at most three natural-language choices.
+   It remains nonterminal unless the user separately confirms
+   `keep_as_follow_up`. Dismiss creates no proposal, memory, task, or work item.
+7. Add revalidates the current version, visible confirmed suggestions, current
+   writer membership, tenant, parent/dependency targets, and destination config.
+   One atomic command creates/reuses one proposal and exactly one work item.
+   Retry returns the same result; stale or ambiguous input leaves the card usable
+   and creates nothing.
+8. The added card becomes terminal and shows one accessible work-item link. It
+   cannot be restored. The user can audit safe provenance links without seeing
+   internal IDs, auth subjects, raw evidence, prompts, or denied counts.
+
+## Exact agent and service flow
+
+1. Capture/finalization services store transcript/final summary evidence under
+   the meeting origin. They never call proposal/work-item or memory writers.
+2. B6 materialization projects the latest final summary and extracted action
+   rows into immutable meeting-owned versions. Refresh is idempotent and never
+   reopens terminal review subjects.
+3. Adjust uses a dedicated tool-free agent run linked to the meeting
+   conversation. Input is limited to subject kind, displayed version, confirmed
+   evidence IDs, and delimited user text—never raw transcript, denied content,
+   retrieval/mutation tools, or a generic workboard prompt.
+4. Server-side strict decoding and evidence filtering occur before one CAS makes
+   a new version current. Model output cannot choose a terminal state or write a
+   work item.
+5. Add is a deterministic server command, not a model tool. The winning
+   transaction repeats current authorization and creates the exact persisted
+   proposal/work result.
+6. A future visual-artifact request starts only from an explicit user or
+   authorized-agent request against a specific meeting/version. It shows type/
+   cost capability, uses Mermaid first, and stores a versioned artifact with
+   evidence/origin; failure never changes candidates.
+7. A future external connector emits only a canonical evidence envelope with
+   source/capability/consent/gap/confidence provenance. Provider/calendar labels
+   never authorize, materialize candidates, or promote work.
+
+## UX acceptance
+
+- Completion is truthful: no success toast/state before durable drain,
+  finalization, and artifact refresh; retryable failures remain actionable.
+- Summary and action cards are distinct discriminated unions. Summary Add is
+  structurally impossible, not hidden by CSS.
+- All controls are native labelled buttons/links. Icons are decorative;
+  keyboard focus enters and leaves inline Adjust predictably; terminal cards
+  expose only valid actions.
+- Stale commands return the latest safe card and preserve the user's draft.
+  Duplicate commands return the persisted result with no duplicate work.
+- `Dismiss -> Restore -> Add` reuses the same pending legacy proposal only under
+  the audited policy; Added can never Restore.
+- No automatic task, proposal, work-item, parent, owner, date, dependency, or
+  memory write occurs from completion, extraction, refresh, Adjust, or visuals.
+- Exact browser proof begins with transcript/finalize, not a pre-seeded action
+  candidate, and ends at the created work-item link.
+
+## Security and data gates
+
+1. **Database:** one Neon project/database/schema, one `packages/db` Drizzle
+   journal/runner, exact contiguous migrations, both recognized histories,
+   least-privilege runtime roles, no Alembic/Supabase live path.
+2. **Identity:** provider subject maps to internal user; meeting source tenant/
+   owner maps durably to internal tenant/user; equality/email/labels/request body
+   never grant access.
+3. **Current authorization:** active org, human actor, active conversation,
+   active membership, same tenant, allowed role are checked on the winning read/
+   mutation; missing/revoked/DB failure denies.
+4. **Projection:** no wildcard/raw-row/whole-row JSON egress; denied resources
+   are removed before counts, ranks, retrieval, model input, logs, or errors.
+5. **Promotion:** Add is expected-version, suggestion-fenced, actor-bound,
+   idempotent, atomic, and produces zero memory delta. Adjust has no mutation
+   tools. Dismiss/Restore have exact terminal CAS rules.
+6. **Finalization:** stable terminal identity, contiguous transcript watermark,
+   one ledger result, no partial artifact publication, sanitized errors.
+7. **Client cache:** the landed TanStack boundary remains memory-only and keyed
+   by principal/org without credentials. This is defense in depth, never server
+   authorization, and is not expanded during B8.
+8. **Evidence:** missing credentials, skipped/zero tests, cleanup failure,
+   timeout, truncated/non-reconstructable output are INCOMPLETE/FAIL.
+
