+## Single self-challenge and correction pass
+
+One challenge pass tested whether the roadmap could still produce a polished
+demo while violating the user's outcome or hiding a dependency:
+
+- **Could B8 be mislabeled as MVP complete?** Yes: B8 proves seeded/materialized
+  review and work promotion, but the terminal plan owns transcript-start
+  completion. Correction: B8 is a prerequisite; terminal PR 2 is the MVP exit.
+- **Could “parallel local durability” become unplanned implementation?** Yes:
+  `d88d...` has no live acceptance/task artifact. Correction: its first packet is
+  `/plan`; only its bounded, non-overlapping implementation may run in parallel.
+- **Could terminal finalization revive Alembic authority?** Yes: its older task
+  list still names an Alembic revision. Correction: DEV is blocked until that
+  task is reconciled to the next canonical `packages/db` migration.
+- **Could cards, visuals, chat, or canvas create duplicate lanes?** Yes.
+  Correction: B8 exclusively owns compact cards; visuals/chat/canvas remain the
+  named post-MVP issues and the current canvas seam stays NO-GO.
+- **Could AI SDK, Cloudflare, or LiveKit silently become domain authority?** Yes
+  if their durability/session features were treated as the system of record.
+  Correction: the adapter boundary and Product-Suite authority gates are
+  explicit and release-blocking.
+
+No second critic loop is planned; further material contradiction requires human
+plan review rather than iterative scope growth.
