+## Entry protocol for every implementation PR
+
+1. Read the owning issue/plan, claim with a distinct actor, and prove the live
+   lease with `forge issue owns`.
+2. Rebase/restack on the exact merged dependency SHA; confirm the GitHub base and
+   diff contain only this child.
+3. Record purpose, acceptance, constraints, edge cases, out-of-scope boundaries,
+   exact file ownership, migration order, and expected RED in the owning issue.
+4. Keep one medium PR: target 300-800 net LOC and at most 18 production files.
+   Stop/split before continuing if exceeded.
+5. Use the child plan's TDD commands and exact-head validation. Missing or
+   incomplete evidence is never PASS.
+6. Stop at the stage checkpoint. This roadmap never grants push, PR, merge, DB
+   apply, release, or post-merge authority.
